 INFORMATION...Increasing likelihood of respiratory symptoms\nand breathing discomfort in active children and adults and people\nwith lung disease, such as asthma. Active children and adults, and\npeople with lung disease, such as asthma, should reduce prolonged\nor heavy outdoor exertion.","ends":"2026-08-19T16:00:00-06:00","severity":"Unknown","areaDesc":"Broomfield, CO; Boulder, CO; Douglas, CO; Larimer, CO; Jefferson, CO; Weld, CO; Denver, CO; Adams, CO; Arapahoe, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.bcd88b1b66192e2d43a08e5556c874386ead632c.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.bcd88b1b66192e2d43a08e5556c874386ead632c.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-19T11:32:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 191132 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 532 AM MDT Wed Aug 19 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Isolated storms today, though chances of stronger storms shift to the south. - Warming and drying trend to end the week, before monsoon moisture attempts to return Sunday into early next week. && .DISCUSSION /Through Tuesday/... Issued at 140 AM MDT Wed Au","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-19T09:13:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Today and tonight... Isolated showers and thunderstorms are expected this afternoon and evening. Temperatures will be near normal this afternoon, with minimum RHs around 20% to 35% across much of the area. No elevated fire weather conditions expected. LONG TERM DISCUSSION...Thursday through Sunday... Warmer and generally drier conditions are expected Thursday and Friday. Temperatures","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"cht01","station_name":"Chatfield at South Platte Reservoir","distance_km":4.5,"soil_temp_5cm_f":81.84,"soil_temp_15cm_f":78.75,"soil_moisture_5cm":null,"soil_moisture_